+**Goal:** get every test in `search.test.js` to pass by fixing the real cause of each failure.
+
+**Steps:**
+1. Run `<TEST_CMD> search.test.js` and record exactly which tests fail and the error for each.
+2. Read the test and the code it exercises (likely the search module, plus any query parsing, indexing, ranking or pagination code it imports). Look out for result ordering that isn't guaranteed, case or whitespace normalisation, off-by-one errors in pagination, and debounce or timer code that needs fake timers. For each failure, decide whether the bug is in the source code or in the test.
+3. Fix the cause. If the source code is wrong, fix the source code. Change the test only when the test itself is wrong, and say why in your report.
+4. Run `search.test.js` again until it passes, and run it 3 times to catch flaky tests. Then run the full suite once to check you didn't break anything else.
